# What ziax/build.sh builds: the upstream Quay image BASE_IMAGE, with the files that the commit being built changes
# since BASE_COMMIT written over it. This branch, ziax/BASE_VERSION, is BASE_COMMIT plus our commits.
#
# The Quay operator deploys the Quay version it was released with, so BASE_VERSION follows the operator man1-prod1 runs
# (startingCSV in cluster-configuration's components/operators/base/quay/project-quay.yaml). Another release means a
# new ziax/<version> branch with new BASE_ values (README.md, "Upgrading Quay").

# quay.io/projectquay/quay:3.18.1's linux/amd64 image, by digest alone: podman and skopeo refuse a reference with both a
# tag and a digest. It is the image man1-prod1 ran before this one.
BASE_IMAGE=quay.io/projectquay/quay@sha256:94c72496110f9fc97f05671d950fa1f8537c9d754c17e1f535e3c1a9039afe3c
BASE_VERSION=3.18.1

# The commit BASE_IMAGE was built from, which is not upstream's v3.18.1 git tag: the image was pushed on 2026-10-13,
# from redhat-3.18 at "PROJQUAY-13566: fix(deps): bump click to 8.3.3". Of the 140 files redhat-3.18 changed after
# the tag that the image holds, all match this commit, and no other commit matches them all. build.sh checks the files
# it writes over against it.
BASE_COMMIT=9d98751fba968512c781ff48e81aa08bb205a6e7

SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/teamziax/thirdparty-quay
IMAGE=quay.io/ziax/quay
